WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.790
Speaker 1: Let's try Mark from New Jersey
instead, Mark from Jersey.

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:04.790
You're on the air.

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:06.390
David, how are you?

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:07.759
I'm doing very well.

00:00:07.759 --> 00:00:09.110
Speaker 2: Awesome.

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:14.019
So I was wondering, you know, in today's current
vaccine situation, there's a lot of misinformation

00:00:14.019 --> 00:00:16.970
that's preventing people from getting vaccines.

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:22.070
But do you think a positive misinformation
campaign could lead to good results, something

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:27.550
like, you know, having bald guys say, oh,
help me regrow my hair and things like that,

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:29.079
almost my status?

00:00:29.079 --> 00:00:33.610
Speaker 1: So, no, I mean, so the answer is
yes, it might work.

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:38.910
I mean, listen, the people who buy the supplements,
the people who do all the crazy, you know,

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:43.000
if you're if you would fall for that, they
probably would at least some of them fall

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:50.070
for, you know, the vaccine regrew my hair,
gave me muscle mass and works like, you know,

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:52.510
an erectile dysfunction pill or whatever.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:56.530
I'm sure it would convince some people, but
I don't think it's a great idea.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:01:00.810
What I what I would be more OK with would
be something like.

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:07.430
Calling it trump juice and marketing it like
a soda, and as I tweeted, I think that would

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:10.170
get some Republicans on board.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:13.750
I tweeted about this earlier this week and
a lot of people latched on to it.

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:15.460
They thought it was a good idea.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:21.330
Start spreading the rumor that Democrats are
glad Republicans aren't getting vaccinated

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:23.360
because that means they're going to die.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:27.979
And then maybe Republicans would be like,
screw you, watch me go and get vaccinated

00:01:27.979 --> 00:01:29.330
like that.

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:34.070
But but straight up lies like it'll regrow
hair I wouldn't be on board with.

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:35.090
Speaker 2: Yeah.

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:39.960
So I know if people were saying Bill Gates
is going to mind control people, but if they

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:44.090
framed it where the vaccine protects you from
Bill Gates mind control like that,

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:46.200
Speaker 1: I totally know what you're saying.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.200
I totally know what you're saying.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.560
It would work for some people.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:50.130
I would just listen.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:54.869
I think it would be more benign to just, hey,
promote it is the Trump vaccine, if that's

00:01:54.869 --> 00:01:55.869
what you believe.

00:01:55.869 --> 00:02:00.370
Trump made the vaccine and Trump took the
vaccine be like Trump.

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:04.200
I think that would basically work as well
as the regrow hair thing.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:11.310
And it feels less obviously dishonest, although
it's still dishonest, but in a less empirically

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:12.310
concerning way.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:13.310
Speaker 2: Right.

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:14.310
Thanks, man.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:15.310
My pleasure.

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:16.310
Speaker 1: My pleasure.

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:18.810
Yeah, there's a lot of work to be done there,
that's for sure.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:21.099
Got to figure out what will work with these
people.

